{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_50092ab295d08c5384cd94ec232132536ce88b99acf3cbf1eccf2602e36e8306", "title": "St. Mary's Mission (Montana)", "text": "The Historic St. Mary’s Mission is a mission established by the Society of Jesus of the Catholic Church; located now on 4th street in modern-day Stevensville, Montana. Founded in 1841 and designed as an ongoing village for Catholic Salish Indians, St. Mary’s was the first permanent settlement made by European descendants in what became the state of Montana. The mission structure was rebuilt in 1866, with it being added to the National Register of Historic Places in 1970.", "score": 36.7028}, {"id": "hp_doc_92c50438e4e3a818c2ab4441abb9454c5a73e49753998655adb4e605a4ab1bc9", "title": "St. Peter's Mission Church and Cemetery", "text": "The St. Peter's Mission Church and Cemetery, also known as St. Peter's Mission and as St. Peter's-By-the-Rock is a historic Roman Catholic mission located on Mission Road 10.5 mi west-northwest of the town of Cascade, Montana, United States. The historic site consists of a wooden church and \"opera house\" and a cemetery. Also on the site are the ruins of a stone parochial school for boys, a stone convent, and several outbuildings.", "score": 28.0381}, {"id": "hp_doc_e584aee9fe3a183dee523eaaeb413912039eb2ba3a06ca0c9486e3c37c3f4c38", "title": "St. Mary's Mission (Kansas)", "text": "The St. Mary's Mission was a Jesuit mission founded in 1847 along the Oregon Trail. The city of St. Marys, Kansas was established around the mission. During the 19th and 20th centuries Native American children were often forced to attend Mission schools like St. Mary's. Potawatomi children were taken from their families in the 1860s and sent to St. Mary's Mission where they were left in the care of White Americans.", "score": 18.1968}], "remaining_searches": 2}
